// expect-error: NITPICK-RESOLVE-010
// expect-error: NITPICK-RESOLVE-010
//
// D-179's two form rules for `error:` declarations. An explicit code is the
// PRELUDE's alone — the system domain and its fixed D-142 values live
// there, and a user constant's code is the compiler's to derive, so
// identity can never be forged to collide with (or impersonate) the system
// family. And where a code may appear at all, it is a bare integer
// literal — a computed code would be an identity decided at runtime.
mod:error_decl;

error:Forged = 4102i32;

error:Computed = 1i32 + 2i32;

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 0i32; };
func:failsafe = int32(tbb32:_~e) { exit 1i32; };
